<% content_for(:page_title) { "How It Works" } %>
<% content_for(:page_subtitle) { "ML pipeline, scoring engine, and prediction methodology" } %>

<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8">

  <!-- Intro -->
  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Overview</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      SparkWatch uses a <strong>Sim-to-Real</strong> architecture: a shared behavioral simulator generates both the
      application data and the ML training data. This guarantees the model understands the exact patterns present in the
      platform — a common pitfall in demo projects where seed scripts and training pipelines drift apart.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Data Flow -->
  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Data Flow</h3>
    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-5 font-mono text-xs text-gray-700 leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto">
      <pre class="whitespace-pre">StudentSimulator (shared behavioral model)
    │
    ├── db/seeds.rb
    │     └── 150 students × 6 cohorts × 15 weeks
    │         └── Activities → EngagementScores → Predictions
    │
    └── lib/tasks/ml.rake
          └── 50,000 labeled samples
                ↓
          RandomForest + StandardScaler
                ↓
          dropout_model.marshal (serialized via Git LFS)
                ↓
          Prediction.generate_for(students)
                ↓
          Dashboard Services (widget-based, memoized)
                ↓
          Stimulus Controllers + Chart.js</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Student Simulator -->
  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Student Simulator</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
      Every student is assigned a <strong>behavioral persona</strong> based on their position in the cohort.
      Each persona defines a base engagement rate, variance, and natural decline over the semester.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
            <th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Persona</th>
            <th class="text-center py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Distribution</th>
            <th class="text-center py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Base Rate</th>
            <th class="text-center py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Variance</th>
            <th class="text-center py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Weekly Decline</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-gray-600">
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
            <td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="inline-block w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-green-500 mr-2"></span>Star Student</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">40%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">115%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">±10%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">5%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
            <td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="inline-block w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-blue-500 mr-2"></span>Engaged</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">35%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">100%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">±15%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">8%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
            <td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="inline-block w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-yellow-500 mr-2"></span>Moderate</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">15%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">80%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">±20%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">12%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
            <td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="inline-block w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-orange-500 mr-2"></span>Inconsistent</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">7%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">60%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">±25%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">20%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="inline-block w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-red-500 mr-2"></span>Disengaged</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">3%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">20%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">±15%</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3">10%</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-3">
      The simulator also models mid-semester slumps, personal trend variations, and random boost/rough weeks for realism.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Engagement Scoring -->
  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Engagement Scoring</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
      Each student receives a <strong>weekly engagement score</strong> on a 0–10,000 integer scale 
      (displayed as 0–100%). The score is a weighted sum of activity completion percentages:
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-5 gap-3 mb-4">
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-indigo-700">30%</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Attendance</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">3 classes/wk</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-indigo-700">30%</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Assignments</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">2 submissions/wk</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-indigo-700">20%</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Quizzes</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">1 quiz/wk</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-indigo-700">10%</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Questions</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">2 questions/wk</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-indigo-700">10%</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Parent Login</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">2 logins/wk</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs">
      Scores are stored as integers (0–10,000) to avoid floating-point drift in aggregations. 
      The <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">EngagementScore.to_percent</code> method converts to display values.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ML Model -->
  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Dropout Prediction Model</h3>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <!-- Model Specs -->
      <div>
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 text-sm mb-3">Model Specification</h4>
        <dl class="space-y-2 text-sm">
          <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
            <dt class="text-gray-500">Algorithm</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium text-gray-900">Random Forest</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
            <dt class="text-gray-500">Estimators</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium text-gray-900">150 trees</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
            <dt class="text-gray-500">Max Depth</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium text-gray-900">10</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
            <dt class="text-gray-500">Max Features</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium text-gray-900">2 per split</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
            <dt class="text-gray-500">Preprocessing</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium text-gray-900">StandardScaler</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
            <dt class="text-gray-500">Training Samples</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium text-gray-900">50,000</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
            <dt class="text-gray-500">Train/Test Split</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium text-gray-900">80/20</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between">
            <dt class="text-gray-500">Label Noise</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium text-gray-900">5% (robustness)</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <!-- Input Features -->
      <div>
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 text-sm mb-3">Input Features</h4>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-3">
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-800 text-sm">Class Attendance %</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Actual classes attended vs. 3 expected per week, capped at 100%</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-3">
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-800 text-sm">Assignment Submission %</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Assignments submitted vs. 2 expected per week, capped at 100%</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-3">
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-800 text-sm">Parent Login %</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Parent logins vs. 2 expected per week, capped at 100%</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-3">
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-800 text-sm">Score Trend (Δ)</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Raw delta between first and last engagement score of the month</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Risk Classification -->
  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Risk Classification</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
      The model outputs a probability of dropout (0–1), which is scaled to a <strong>risk score</strong> (0–10,000).
      Students are then classified into three risk tiers:
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg p-4 bg-red-50 border border-red-200 text-center">
        <p class="text-lg font-bold text-red-700">High Risk</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-red-600 mt-1">≥ 90%</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">Immediate intervention recommended</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg p-4 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 text-center">
        <p class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Medium Risk</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-amber-600 mt-1">75% – 89%</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">Monitor closely, proactive outreach</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg p-4 bg-green-50 border border-green-200 text-center">
        <p class="text-lg font-bold text-green-700">Low Risk</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-green-600 mt-1">< 75%</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">On track, standard monitoring</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Explainability -->
  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Prediction Explainability</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">
      Every prediction includes a <strong>per-feature breakdown</strong> stored as JSONB. This shows the raw input
      values that drove each prediction, making it possible to explain <em>why</em> a student was flagged:
    </p>
    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-700">
      <pre class="whitespace-pre">{
  "class_attended":        83,   ← 83% of expected classes
  "assignment_submitted":  50,   ← 50% of expected assignments
  "parent_login":          25,   ← 25% of expected parent logins
  "score_trend":         -340    ← engagement score dropped by 340 points
}</pre>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-3">
      This breakdown powers the "Why this prediction?" section on the Student Detail page,
      showing exactly which activity dimensions contributed to a student's risk score.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Training Labels -->
  <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Training Labels</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">
      Labels are derived from the student's behavioral persona:
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
            <th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Persona</th>
            <th class="text-center py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Label</th>
            <th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Rationale</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-gray-600">
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
            <td class="py-2 px-3">Star Student, Engaged, Moderate</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3"><span class="px-2 py-0.5 bg-green-100 text-green-800 rounded-full text-xs font-medium">Low Risk</span></td>
            <td class="py-2 px-3">Sufficient engagement to persist</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 px-3">Inconsistent, Disengaged</td>
            <td class="text-center py-2 px-3"><span class="px-2 py-0.5 bg-red-100 text-red-800 rounded-full text-xs font-medium">High Risk</span></td>
            <td class="py-2 px-3">Behavioral pattern correlated with dropout</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-3">
      5% of labels are randomly flipped during training to introduce noise, preventing the model from overfitting
      to the deterministic persona-to-label mapping.
    </p>
  </div>

</div>
